.TH STOP-MU2E-RUNDB-VIEWER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-runlog-db t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2e-rundb-viewer \- stop the Mu2e run-log web viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads
.I .runserver.pid
next to the script.
If the file is absent, or names a process that is not running, it says so,
removes a stale file, and exits 0.
Otherwise it sends SIGTERM, waits up to 10 seconds, sends SIGKILL if the
process is still alive, and removes the PID file.
For gunicorn the PID is the master, which stops its workers.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
Arguments are accepted and ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .runserver.pid
Written by
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 in all normal cases.
Non-zero only if
.B kill
fails, for example when the process belongs to another user.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
\&./stop\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
